Quoting  Justin Chase  <justncase80@gmail.com>:
>a.) Yes I could translate it into C# / XNA.

Yes, _but_ you could not release it in the X-Box Arcade or whatever unless
you were in a position to make the full source code of your modified
version available to anyone who wanted it. Furthermore it would have to be
available _via the same distribution mechanism_ if you proposed to charge
for it.

I will bet that the X-Box thingy, being Microsoft, will explicitly forbid
you from distributing programs under Free licenses similar to the GPL
(the NetHack license is a cousin to the GPL being derived from the Bison
license).

>b.) No, you cannot charge for it, even for $1.

Wrong, but charging imposes additional requirements under para 3, and you
cannot prohibit any recipient from distributing your modified version for
free.
